{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-linear time-series systems are notoriously difficult to forecast. "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Koopman Operator Theory"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" maps non-linear state spaces into an infinite-dimensional Hilbert space where the dynamics evolve linearly:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"$$g(x_{k+1}) = \\mathcal{K} , g(x_k)$$"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftForecast","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" implements "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Extended Dynamic Mode Decomposition (EDMD)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" to approximate the Koopman operator matrix $\\mathbf{K}$ using a set of non-linear dictionary observable functions (e.g., polynomials, RBF kernels)."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"1-Fitting-an-EDMD-Model","text":"1. Fitting an EDMD Model","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ Initialize Koopman Operator with polynomial dictionary observables","let edmd = ExtendedDynamicModeDecomposition(degree: 3)","","let trajectory = [1.0, 1.414, 2.0, 2.828, 4.0, 5.656, 8.0]","try await edmd.fit(trajectory: trajectory)","","\/\/ Predict future states linearly in observable space","let futureSteps = try await edmd.predict(steps: 5)","print(\"Forecasted states: \\(futureSteps)\")"]}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/spectralanalysisandedmd"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}],"title":"Koopman Operator Theory & Spectral Decomposition","role":"collectionGroup"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SpectralAnalysisAndEDMD","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model non-linear dynamical systems using linear infinite-dimensional Koopman operator embeddings."}],"references":{"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast","abstract":[{"text":"Time Series & Volatility Forecasting Models.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast","title":"SwiftForecast"}}}